{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition","id":1491483,"title":"Did they explain the emotion problems in the 2nd edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-27T09:47:28-07:00","id":1491483,"title":"Did they explain the emotion problems in the 2nd edition?","content":"I remember that poorly worded section in the 1st edition on how Kindred don't really feel emotions at all. What they had were echoes of what they felt when they were alive. That bit could have been explained better or not added at all inhmo. Did the 2nd edition do away with that problem at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T11:40:10-07:00","id":1491504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition#post1491483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that poorly worded section in the 1st edition on how Kindred don't really feel emotions at all. What they had were echoes of what they felt when they were alive. That bit could have been explained better or not added at all inhmo. Did the 2nd edition do away with that problem at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was due to the lack of a soul, if memory deserves, which is not anymore a thing in 2ed. So you have kindred with emotions and able to create art!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T12:02:44-07:00","id":1491506,"title":"","content":"Blood Sympathy can trigger on any intense emotion, a major part of the Daeva's schtick is being emotionally intense, and one of the sample Strix is specifically possessing a vampire to try and get a handle on Kindred emotions. It's not present in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T13:20:15-07:00","id":1491514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1491506#post1491506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Sympathy can trigger on any intense emotion, a major part of the Daeva's schtick is being emotionally intense, and one of the sample Strix is specifically possessing a vampire to try and get a handle on Kindred emotions. It's not present in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>... or that other vamps, beside Daeva - are at least a bit 'emotional dull'. Daeva then 'shine' in Kindred society as 'too human-like' compared to other Clans, for their own Bane...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T13:54:16-07:00","id":1491516,"title":"","content":"Yup, full emotions. And for me, all the talk of the predatory aura and the blood bond and the All Night Society makes me think they actually have the opposite problem; <i>too much</i> emotion, but just focused on the Id part of the mind. The Beast might as well be a psychically supercharged Id as some vampires reckon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T09:22:03-07:00","id":1491772,"title":"","content":"What is a Strix? I heard it mentioned before in some of the other posts. Is it some sort of spirit that likes to plague the Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T13:00:12-07:00","id":1491804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1491772#post1491772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a Strix? I heard it mentioned before in some of the other posts. Is it some sort of spirit that likes to plague the Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampiric bodyjackers who variously resent the Kindred's attachment to Humanity, claim to be responsible for the Beast, and cause trouble in the pursuit of their assorted agendas and hedonistic desires. There's a Strix who possesses dead animals, there's a Strix that trying to create a new clan to arguably very low levels of success, there's a Strix who uses photography to steal people's souls, there's a Strix who's a master of Cr\u00faac, and many more besides.<br /> <br /> They're made of smoke and shadows and are very difficult to kill. Lot of owl imagery associated with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T16:08:53-07:00","id":1491825,"title":"","content":"Oh that sounds like a lot of unneeded complications in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T16:29:17-07:00","id":1491830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1491825#post1491825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh that sounds like a lot of unneeded complications in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a more meta sense, the Strix are to vampires what vampires are to humans, so there\u2019s a use for them in that aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T16:33:20-07:00","id":1491831,"title":"","content":"Now that sounds more fitting with what vampires are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T16:54:07-07:00","id":1491833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1491825#post1491825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh that sounds like a lot of unneeded complications in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The list of example characters? They're example characters.<br /> <br /> They exist to be boogeymen who can throw an additional wrench into the already-fraught power dynamics of a vampiric domain inhabited by undead predators who struggle to maintain perspective with the living as a form of self-preservation.<br /> <br /> They're there to be a natural enemy to the Friendly Neighborhood Vampire by confronting them with What Vampires Are and messing with their carefully-kept feeding practices and sabotaging their precious mortal relationships.<br /> <br /> They're one of the most recurring forms of Inhuman Vampire in the setting and the ones that don't hate you on principle still might fuck around with your Herd because they think it'd be funny and they have nothing but time on their claws.<br /> <br /> They are <i>specifically</i> there to be a complication. &quot;The Strix Chronicle&quot; was the original subtitle of Blood and Smoke for the same reason that &quot;The Idigam Chronicle&quot; was Werewolf 2e's original ready-made Big Story Hook: these things upset the apple cart of an otherwise stable-looking setting, whether through fomenting paranoia about infiltrators or doing big horrifying body-horror scenes or poisoning valuable resources for petty or incomprehensible reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T17:22:39-07:00","id":1491838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1491831#post1491831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that sounds more fitting with what vampires are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another design point is that if the Kindred are Dracula and Carmilla and the pop culture image that emerged thereforth, the strix are the ghoulish stalking monsters of traditional folklorish vampiric creatures.<br /> <br /> The strix, notably, occupy the role of a &quot;sample spotlight antagonist.&quot; They're showstoppers for big chronicle events. They're <i>optional </i>in this sense. Lots of Vampire chronicles can play out without ever having a strix make an appearance. (And the existence of the strix can be a plot point without any strix actually ever being present, too; the Strix Chronicle Anthology features one short story where a Prince's unfounded paranoia destroys a domain.)<br /> <br /> They were introduced in 1e through Requiem for Rome and a subplot running through the clanbooks, as an original sin for Clan Julii, a suggested spectre haunting the history of the Kindred, and a returning curse to visit the sins of the father upon the child. Clan Julii is extinct... or are they? Why do the strix still carry a grudge?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T05:25:49-07:00","id":1492088,"title":"","content":"I think the most important thing about the Strix (is there a rule on pluralizing strix? I know sometimes the actual word strix is plural to striges...) is what Stupid Loserman said: they thematically complete Vampire. If Kindred are pop vampires and, like pop vampires, introspective (&quot;What does it mean to me now that I'm a monster who has to hurt people to survive? Am I actually a worse person than I was?&quot;), Strix offer an opportunity to play the paranoid victims of a vampire story, while still playing as vampires! Previously, that space was filled by particularly insane Kindred, but they were still Kindred. They were people within a society bucking those rules. They weren't creatures from outside a society infiltrating and preying upon that society. <br /> <br /> Secondly, the Strix are actually very easy to &quot;slow-drip&quot; into a Chronicle. An important scene is accompanied by unintrusive mentions of dark owls perched on power lines. As a character leaves a scene, their eyes flash yellow in the streetlights. Eventually these little sparks of oddness start to add up to some seriously effective atmosphere. My players did catch on the eye thing earlier than I thought: I guess having the Strix possess a vampire with stunning blue eyes may have been a bit obvious, the players clearly remembered her eye colour!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T15:30:32-07:00","id":1492122,"title":"","content":"Strix are pretty cool. In my current Tokyo campaign i'm using the Black Cat Strix from the core book as a little devil working with the local Belial Brood as a recruter. Being rather inoffensives as far as strix goes, he's just their taunting the Mekhet Ume Priest with secrets in exchange for beastly actions. Players are starding to get rather fond of him even though he's mostly a nuisance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T09:16:09-07:00","id":1492306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1492088#post1492088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the most important thing about the Strix (is there a rule on pluralizing strix? I know sometimes the actual word strix is plural to striges...) is what Stupid Loserman said: they thematically complete Vampire. If Kindred are pop vampires and, like pop vampires, introspective (&quot;What does it mean to me now that I'm a monster who has to hurt people to survive? Am I actually a worse person than I was?&quot;), Strix offer an opportunity to play the paranoid victims of a vampire story, while still playing as vampires! Previously, that space was filled by particularly insane Kindred, but they were still Kindred. They were people within a society bucking those rules. They weren't creatures from outside a society infiltrating and preying upon that society.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Strix are actually very easy to &quot;slow-drip&quot; into a Chronicle. An important scene is accompanied by unintrusive mentions of dark owls perched on power lines. As a character leaves a scene, their eyes flash yellow in the streetlights. Eventually these little sparks of oddness start to add up to some seriously effective atmosphere. My players did catch on the eye thing earlier than I thought: I guess having the Strix possess a vampire with stunning blue eyes may have been a bit obvious, the players clearly remembered her eye colour!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(plural </span></span></span><b>striges</b><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> or </span></span></span><b>strixes</b><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(mythology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(mythology</a>)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T11:02:28-07:00","id":1492532,"title":"","content":"If you're going to make ancient Rome relevant to the backstory of Vampire, you might as well include what the ancient Romans actually thought vampires were.<br /> <br /> First Edition was going with an idea that vampires were kind of stuck at the point where their life ended. I think it worked for what it was, but the modification for Second Edition is certainly part of a more sophisticated milieu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T13:14:48-07:00","id":1534265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition#post1491483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that poorly worded section in the 1st edition on how Kindred don't really feel emotions at all. What they had were echoes of what they felt when they were alive. That bit could have been explained better or not added at all inhmo. Did the 2nd edition do away with that problem at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's be real here, even 1e did away with that and fairly early on too. It was fluff in the corebook that never got followed up on. You can easily handwave it. When I would ST Requiem, vampires always had the same full range of emotions and we never did anything with Predator's Taint. Yeah, Kindred often had a sixth sense of knowing when other vampires were around but we never called for frenzy checks or anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T16:58:06-07:00","id":1538931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1534265#post1534265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's be real here, even 1e did away with that and fairly early on too. It was fluff in the corebook that never got followed up on. You can easily handwave it. When I would ST Requiem, vampires always had the same full range of emotions and we never did anything with Predator's Taint. Yeah, Kindred often had a sixth sense of knowing when other vampires were around but we never called for frenzy checks or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Vampires have no emotions&quot; is one of the things that always appear patently false to me in every setting I can think of now. VtM, VtR 1e, VtR 2e, as well as stories, books, movies, etc... vampires are way too full of emotions. And their stories would be very boring if they weren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T18:46:54-07:00","id":1538934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1538931#post1538931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Vampires have no emotions&quot; is one of the things that always appear patently false to me in every setting I can think of now. VtM, VtR 1e, VtR 2e, as well as stories, books, movies, etc... vampires are way too full of emotions. And their stories would be very boring if they weren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It was some fluff in the 1e corebook that was honestly nonsensical and came off as trying too hard.<br /> <br /> To be honest. I think it was probably shoehorned in as a hamfisted and poorly thought-out way to try and force some sort of weird sense of thematic purity and prevent those icky &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas&quot; players from having badwrongfun.<br /> <br /> A lot of the WW writers at that time unfortunately had a bad habit of getting really worked up at people potentially &quot;playing the game wrong&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T05:17:59-07:00","id":1538942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1491483-did-they-explain-the-emotion-problems-in-the-2nd-edition?p=1538934#post1538934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. It was some fluff in the 1e corebook that was honestly nonsensical and came off as trying too hard.<br /> <br /> To be honest. I think it was probably shoehorned in as a hamfisted and poorly thought-out way to try and force some sort of weird sense of thematic purity and prevent those icky &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas&quot; players from having badwrongfun.<br /> <br /> A lot of the WW writers at that time unfortunately had a bad habit of getting really worked up at people potentially &quot;playing the game wrong&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's just that, I think it is a repeated theme in vampire stories to portray them as more dead and alien and give their thirst for blood and attachment to specific victims a sort of &quot;emotional hunger&quot; vibe to it... but it just doesn't work, that's the issue. I don't think it's even easy to <i>imagine</i> characters without emotions, vampiric or otherwise, let alone to write stories about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}